invariant: INV-16
file: src/chacha20_vector.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh vector-neon
reason: the NEON block in general registers takes the counter of the
  last block of the second group, so a pass computes one keystream block
  twice and skips the next: an in-place record XORs the same 64 bytes of
  keystream into two blocks. bin/chacha20_equiv_test compares every byte
  of the output with chacha20.c's, at every length that reaches the block.

--- old
    uint32_t scalar_counter = counter + (uint32_t)(PASS_GROUPS * GROUP_BLOCKS);
--- new
    uint32_t scalar_counter = counter + (uint32_t)(PASS_GROUPS * GROUP_BLOCKS - 1);
